findings.body:
The head commit changed the `RolloutsSettingMessage` comment from `%@` to `%1$@`, but the `value` still uses `%@`.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Shared/Strings.swift" lines="6257-6261"}

The sibling `StudiesSettingMessageV3` documents `%@` in both value and comment. `%@` and `%1$@` are equivalent for a single-argument `String(format:)`, so this won't break at runtime, but the comment now misdescribes the format specifier and is inconsistent with the Studies string added in the same diff — which can confuse translators matching positional specifiers. Keep the comment on `%@`.
